PoolKit third-party notices

PoolKit includes data from GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org): the
cities15000 table, trimmed to each city's id, name, country code, latitude and
longitude. GeoNames data is
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

PoolKit includes a prebuilt SentencePiece library from swift-sentencepiece, licensed under the MIT License.

PoolKit's interest taxonomy maps its topics to ids from
the IAB Tech Lab Audience Taxonomy 1.1 (https://iabtechlab.com/standards/audience-taxonomy/),
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/). The topic names, groupings and
labels are Pool's own.

PoolKit is built with these open source packages, compiled into the framework:
GRDB.swift (MIT, Gwendal Roué), sqlite-data, swift-structured-queries,
swift-dependencies, swift-sharing, swift-perception, swift-identified-collections,
swift-custom-dump, swift-issue-reporting, swift-concurrency-extras,
swift-clocks and combine-schedulers (MIT, Point-Free, Inc.), and
swift-async-algorithms and swift-collections (Apache License 2.0, Apple Inc.).
The MIT License: https://opensource.org/license/mit. The Apache License 2.0:
